{
 "thread": "w1wMKjz9xcU",
 "subject": "more than one widget in renderUI?",
 "messages_listed": 7,
 "last_activity": "2015-05-19T01:19:03Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "yCDxjBXGscYJ",
   "from": "Norman Packard",
   "author": "8e72bac5f7bfb16e",
   "date": "2015-05-16T02:16:59Z",
   "subject": "more than one widget in renderUI?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div>I would like to have a dynamic UI element that puts up more than one widget.<div>Is this possible?</div><div>I tried the most straightforward thing (in server.R):<br><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    output$foo &lt;- renderUI({</font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">        sliderInput(&#39;a&#39;,&quot;a description&quot;,min=0,max=200,value=c(50,150))</span><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">        sliderInput(&#39;b&#39;,&quot;b description&quot;,min=0,max=200,value=c(50,150))</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    })</font></div></div><div><br></div><div>and I see only one slider.  Turns out:  the &#39;b&#39; one. </div></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks for any help!!!</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M6B-ktCwW_gJ",
   "from": "Norman Packard",
   "author": "8e72bac5f7bfb16e",
   "date": "2015-05-16T02:34:20Z",
   "subject": "Re: more than one widget in renderUI?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div>Found the solution!</div><div>Thanks to <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msg/shiny-discuss/xW8f5g5gm4s/_2TA5S_2HV4J\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msg/shiny-discuss/xW8f5g5gm4s/_2TA5S_2HV4J&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792398758581000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3tHozO_VS4XuUwIjXoonpf\">Herman Sontrop</a>.</div><div><br></div><div>The key is putting the widgets into a list:</div><div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">output$foo &lt;- renderUI({</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">        LL = list()</font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">        LL[[1]] = list(sliderInput(&#39;a&#39;,&quot;a description&quot;,min=0,max=200,value=c(50,150)))</span><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">        LL[[2]] = list(sliderInput(&#39;b&#39;,&quot;b description&quot;,min=0,max=200,value=c(50,150)))</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">        return(LL)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    })</font></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "6BNcJlE6ZlUJ",
   "from": "Dean Attali",
   "author": "a1bf76ab9a5a2d4b",
   "date": "2015-05-16T03:36:15Z",
   "subject": "Re: more than one widget in renderUI?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">That&#39;s one way. You could also just wrap everything in a tag, such as a div<div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace;color:rgb(34,34,34);background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">output$foo </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> renderUI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code><div style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">        div(<br></font><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">          sliderInput(&#39;a&#39;,&quot;a description&quot;,min=0,max=200,</span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">value=c(50,150)),</span></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">          sliderInput(&#39;b&#39;,&quot;b description&quot;,min=0,max=200,value=c(50,150))<br>        )</font></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><div style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    })</font></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br><br>On Friday, 15 May 2015 19:34:20 UTC-7, Norman Packard  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div>Found the solution!</div><div>Thanks to <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msg/shiny-discuss/xW8f5g5gm4s/_2TA5S_2HV4J\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msg/shiny-discuss/xW8f5g5gm4s/_2TA5S_2HV4J&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792398758582000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Zq3vd7MzWNTvlbx0bsNGS\">Herman Sontrop</a>.</div><div><br></div><div>The key is putting the widgets into a list:</div><div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">output$foo &lt;- renderUI({</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">        LL = list()</font></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">        LL[[1]] = list(sliderInput(&#39;a&#39;,&quot;a description&quot;,min=0,max=200,value=c(50,150)))</span><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">        LL[[2]] = list(sliderInput(&#39;b&#39;,&quot;b description&quot;,min=0,max=200,value=c(50,150)))</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">        return(LL)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    })</font></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ebxfrb6wYv0J",
   "from": "Norman Packard",
   "author": "8e72bac5f7bfb16e",
   "date": "2015-05-16T23:50:43Z",
   "subject": "Re: more than one widget in renderUI?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Dean!  This seems cleaner.<div><br></div><div>However, if the number of sliders (and their content) is computed on the fly, perhaps the list works best?</div><div><br></div><div>I tried putting a bunch of <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">sliderIntputs()</font> inside a loop inside a <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">div</font>, and it didn&#39;t seem to work.</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "W6VR4IEfLlgJ",
